    {
      "id": 74232,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-09-23T06:34:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Presumably the five villains will each have a deck of their own, although possibly not the full 25.&nbsp; But even if there was only a single 25-card villain deck, that plus two Environments and five 40-card Heroes totals 255 non-character cards (and seven character ones), compared to 210 (and ten characters) for the $20 expansions.&nbsp; If all of the villains have full-size decks, that adds another 100 cards (plus eight more characters), and it's no longer remotely close.&nbsp; The EE is $40, and it contains 500+ cards, but its price was probably low-rolled a little bit for the sake of getting people into the game; the expansions probably have a higher profit margin so that they don't need to sell in comparable volume.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:54:10.687Z",
